evil, then I will relent of the disaster I had planned to bring.","from":3},{"book":"JER","chapter":30,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"“This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Write in a book all the words that I have spoken to you.","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":3,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Repent, then, and turn back, so that your sins may be wiped away,","from":3},{"book":"EXO","chapter":17,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then the LORD said to Moses, “Write this on a scroll as a reminder and recite it to Joshua, because I will utterly blot out the memory of Amalek from under heaven.”","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":30,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and when you and your children return to the LORD your God and obey His voice with all your heart and all your soul according to everything I am giving you today,","from":3},{"book":"JER","chapter":1,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"See, I have appointed you today over nations and kingdoms to uproot and tear down, to destroy and overthrow, to build and plant.”","from":2},{"book":"JER","chapter":25,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"This is the word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the people of Judah in the fourth year of Jehoiakim son of Josiah king of Judah, which was the first year of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon.","from":1},{"book":"JER","chapter":25,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“From the thirteenth year of Josiah son of Amon king of Judah until this very day—twenty-three years—the word of the LORD has come to me, and I have spoken to you again and again, but you have not listened.","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exile-prophets","title":"Last kings of Judah and the prophets of the exile","people":4},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs",